1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:04,380
Every day, somebody gets asked to prove one small thing.

2
00:00:04,820 --> 00:00:07,080
A shop wants to know if you are over 18.

3
00:00:07,080 --> 00:00:09,310
A bank wants to know that the name on the form

4
00:00:09,310 --> 00:00:11,080
belongs to a verified person.

5
00:00:11,240 --> 00:00:12,890
The question is a yes or a no.

6
00:00:13,040 --> 00:00:15,672
What you hand over is your whole ID, and it gets

7
00:00:15,672 --> 00:00:20,230
photographed, saved, and forwarded, and every copy is somewhere your details

8
00:00:20,230 --> 00:00:21,555
can leak from later.

9
00:00:21,555 --> 00:00:23,320
SabiID is a broker.

10
00:00:23,320 --> 00:00:27,090
It sits between the identity sources and the people checking identity,

11
00:00:27,120 --> 00:00:29,520
and it passes back the answer alone.

12
00:00:29,520 --> 00:00:32,960
One question should cost one answer, not your whole record.

13
00:00:33,420 --> 00:00:35,460
This is the citizen's own phone.

14
00:00:35,460 --> 00:00:38,590
Adaeze enrolled once with her NIN and her BVN.

15
00:00:38,620 --> 00:00:41,410
What she got back is a credential signed by the gateway,

16
00:00:41,410 --> 00:00:44,160
and its body holds only salted hashes of her claims, not

17
00:00:44,260 --> 00:00:45,380
the claims themselves.

18
00:00:45,620 --> 00:00:48,440
Her name, her date of birth, her state, they live here

19
00:00:48,440 --> 00:00:50,400
on the device and nowhere else.

20
00:00:50,420 --> 00:00:53,300
She can reveal a value to herself, like her date of birth.

21
00:00:53,300 --> 00:00:56,400
Nobody else sees any of it unless she chooses to send it.

22
00:00:56,400 --> 00:00:58,200
The record stays with the person.

23
00:00:58,310 --> 00:01:00,870
The gateway keeps a signature, not a copy.

24
00:01:01,220 --> 00:01:05,230
Now a bank wants to open an account for her.

25
00:01:05,260 --> 00:01:08,600
Instead of asking for the ID, it asks three narrow things.

26
00:01:08,620 --> 00:01:10,370
Is this a verified identity.

27
00:01:10,440 --> 00:01:11,598
Is she over 18.

28
00:01:11,598 --> 00:01:13,940
Does the name on our form match.

29
00:01:13,960 --> 00:01:15,890
It never asks for the date of birth, and it never

30
00:01:16,020 --> 00:01:17,080
asks for the address.

31
00:01:17,260 --> 00:01:19,933
It sends that short list to Adaeze and waits for her

32
00:01:19,933 --> 00:01:21,280
to approve it on her phone.

33
00:01:21,300 --> 00:01:23,610
The bank asks for the least it can get away with,

34
00:01:23,610 --> 00:01:24,430
not the most.

35
00:01:24,920 --> 00:01:27,900
Here is the request on Adaeze's phone.

36
00:01:27,920 --> 00:01:30,130
She sees every field the bank wants.

37
00:01:30,290 --> 00:01:34,210
She approves being a verified identity, and she approves being over 18.

38
00:01:34,210 --> 00:01:36,770
She unticks the name check, because she does not want to

39
00:01:36,770 --> 00:01:38,770
confirm the exact spelling this time.

40
00:01:38,850 --> 00:01:41,900
She confirms it is her with a code from her SIM.

41
00:01:41,900 --> 00:01:45,440
Whatever she did not tick is simply withheld.

42
00:01:45,440 --> 00:01:48,640
Consent here is field by field, and she holds the switch.

43
00:01:48,640 --> 00:01:52,140
Nothing is shared until she taps approve, and only what she taps.

44
00:01:52,720 --> 00:01:54,910
This is everything the bank receives.

45
00:01:55,320 --> 00:01:57,520
Yes, it is a verified identity.

46
00:01:57,520 --> 00:01:59,560
Yes, she is over 18.

47
00:01:59,560 --> 00:02:02,780
The name check is withheld, because she chose not to answer it.

48
00:02:02,780 --> 00:02:06,340
There is no date of birth anywhere in this response.

49
00:02:06,340 --> 00:02:09,340
The answer carries a signature from the gateway, and the bank

50
00:02:09,340 --> 00:02:14,050
checks that signature right here in the browser against the gateway's public key.

51
00:02:14,050 --> 00:02:15,530
It needs nothing from us.

52
00:02:15,620 --> 00:02:19,440
Then a hospital asks for a genotype, which nobody has verified.

53
00:02:19,440 --> 00:02:20,830
The gateway does not guess.

54
00:02:20,910 --> 00:02:23,660
It says so, and points to where it can be done.

55
00:02:23,660 --> 00:02:27,480
A signed yes or no, verifiable on the partner's own machine,

56
00:02:27,480 --> 00:02:29,940
and honest about what it does not know.

57
00:02:31,020 --> 00:02:34,600
Every question through the gateway is one line here, and each

58
00:02:34,600 --> 00:02:37,000
line carries the hash of the line before it.

59
00:02:37,020 --> 00:02:41,110
A line holds a pseudonymous ID, the partner, the fields asked,

60
00:02:41,110 --> 00:02:42,000
and the outcomes.

61
00:02:42,020 --> 00:02:46,000
It never holds a date of birth, an address, or a biometric.

62
00:02:46,020 --> 00:02:49,000
We press verify and every line checks out.

63
00:02:49,020 --> 00:02:52,000
Now we quietly edit one past line.

64
00:02:52,130 --> 00:02:55,090
Verify points straight at it and says it was changed after

65
00:02:55,280 --> 00:02:56,000
it was written.

66
00:02:56,020 --> 00:02:59,020
We put it back, and the chain is whole again.

67
00:02:59,020 --> 00:03:02,860
The log proves a check happened, and it cannot be rewritten

68
00:03:02,860 --> 00:03:05,000
later without the edit showing.

69
00:03:06,120 --> 00:03:09,180
This is the same mechanism, asked every month.

70
00:03:09,200 --> 00:03:12,640
Before this ministry pays, SabiID asks each line one thing.

71
00:03:12,640 --> 00:03:15,520
Is this still the same living person we enrolled.

72
00:03:15,520 --> 00:03:18,970
The staff who answer with a fresh face check are paid.

73
00:03:19,080 --> 00:03:20,500
Five lines are held.

74
00:03:20,520 --> 00:03:23,220
One has no NIN record and was never a person.

75
00:03:23,520 --> 00:03:27,420
One is listed as deceased at the Civil Registration service.

76
00:03:27,480 --> 00:03:29,620
One has relocated and stopped answering.

77
00:03:29,640 --> 00:03:32,100
One offered a sample that did not match.

78
00:03:32,100 --> 00:03:34,290
And one is a real staff member who was just out

79
00:03:34,410 --> 00:03:35,880
of network signal.

80
00:03:35,880 --> 00:03:38,920
The system cannot tell that last one from a ghost, so

81
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:40,560
it sends them to a human.

82
00:03:40,640 --> 00:03:45,960
On this run it pays about 1.4 million naira and holds back 955,000.

83
00:03:45,960 --> 00:03:49,410
The audit line becomes the reason a payment was stopped, and

84
00:03:49,500 --> 00:03:52,370
a real person still gets a human's second look.

85
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:57,280
Power cuts and dropped networks are normal here, so we built for them.

86
00:03:57,460 --> 00:04:01,130
We run the payroll with the identity sources offline. Nothing pays.

87
00:04:01,130 --> 00:04:02,480
Every line is queued.

88
00:04:02,480 --> 00:04:05,860
When the link comes back, one reconcile step replays the queue,

89
00:04:05,860 --> 00:04:08,970
and the log records the outage and the recovery as their own lines.

90
00:04:09,920 --> 00:04:11,200
The chain still verifies across the gap.

91
00:04:11,200 --> 00:04:14,200
And for the citizen with a basic phone and weak signal,

92
00:04:14,220 --> 00:04:17,620
the same approvals work over a USSD short code.

93
00:04:17,650 --> 00:04:21,170
They dial in, see the check waiting, approve it, and view

94
00:04:21,170 --> 00:04:22,300
their last few checks.

95
00:04:22,300 --> 00:04:24,830
The face step is skipped on a feature phone, and the

96
00:04:24,830 --> 00:04:26,380
person is told it was skipped.

97
00:04:26,380 --> 00:04:28,960
It keeps working when the lights go off, and it does

98
00:04:28,960 --> 00:04:31,800
not shut out the person without a smartphone.
